SUMMARY:2025 5th Square Holiday Party + Annual Urbanist Awards Ceremony
DESCRIPTION:Join 5th Square Advocacy for our Holiday Party + Urbanist Award
 s Ceremony at Indy Hall\, 709 N 2nd StFriday\, December 12th at 7 PMWe wil
 l be presenting awards to members of our community for their outstanding c
 ontributions to Philadelphia’s urbanist movement.5th Square Advocacy is 
 a grassroots nonprofit organization working to advance a vision of a more 
 accessible\, sustainable\, and equitable Philadelphia for all residents. W
 e are building a coalition for better public transit\, better public space
 s\, safer streets and more homes of all shapes and sizes -- for all our ne
 ighbors.Come celebrate with other Philadelphia built environment activists
 \, neighborhood and community leaders\, architects\, planners\, builders\,
  and sustainability advocates at the urbanist holiday party of the season!
 Drinks and light fare will be served.Announcing the 2025 Urbanist Award Wi
 nners!🏅 Urbanist Lifetime Achievement Award - Job Itzkowitz\, Executive
  Director\, Old City District🚍 Urbanist Changemaker of the Year - Joi W
 ashington\, Mayor-Elect\, Media Borough🏛 Public Servant of the Year - M
 olly Hartman\, Senior Policy Director for CM Landau🛴 Advocacy Partner o
 f the Year - Stephen Bronskill\, Coalition Manager\, Transit Forward Phila
 delphia🚲 Neighborhood Champion - Ashlei Tracy\, President\, Fishtown Ne
 ighbors Association🏙 Best Development of the Year - Calder Gardens🌈B
 est Public Space Improvement of the Year - Ashley Lepera\, LeCount Street 
 Reversal Organizer📰 Urbanist Media Champion - Alan Fisher\, Armchair Ur
 banist Series Creator🏆 5th Square Volunteer of the Year - Morgan Allgro
 ve-Hodges\, Transit Committee Co-ChairThis event is all ages and ADA Acces
 sible.Children are welcome at this event for free with a chaperone. At the
  party\, we will also be raffling off the following items to lucky ticket 
 holders!$250 Value: 5-Day "Clubhouse Card" for Coworking at the Indy Hall 
 Clubhouse$100 Gift Card to Fiorella Pasta at 817 Christian Street$25 Value
 : Transit app - 12-month Royale subscription in 2026 Public & Active Trans
 portation:L-Line (Market-Frankford Line) to Spring Garden StationG-Line (1
 5 Trolley) is a 10 minute walk awayBus routes: 5\, 25\, 43\, 57Indego Stat
 ion and Bicycle Racks on 2nd & Brown\n\nDetails & registration: https://5t
 hsq.app.neoncrm.com/np/clients/5thsq/event.jsp?event=6
LOCATION:Indy Hall\, 709 N 2nd St 3rd Floor\, Philadelphia\, PA 19123
URL:https://5thsq.app.neoncrm.com/np/clients/5thsq/event.jsp?event=6
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
